  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q30-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "30",
    "prompt": "Let $P(12,6)$ lie on $y=f(x)$. Find the new coordinates of $P$ on each of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q30-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=2f\\left(\\frac{x+1}{2}\\right)+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(23,13)$",
          "worked": "The original point gives $f(12)=6$. For the new point $(X,Y)$, set the argument of $f$ equal to $12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{X+1}{2}&=12\\\\X+1&=24\\\\X&=23\\\\Y&=2(6)+1\\\\Y&=13\\end{align*}$$\nThe new coordinates are $(23,13)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q30-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-f(2-x)+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-10,-4)$",
          "worked": "Using $f(12)=6$, the new point $(X,Y)$ satisfies\n$$\\begin{align*}2-X&=12\\\\X&=-10\\\\Y&=-6+2\\\\Y&=-4\\end{align*}$$\nThe new coordinates are $(-10,-4)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q30-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac12 f\\left(\\frac{x}{2}-3\\right)-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(30,0)$",
          "worked": "Using $f(12)=6$, the new point $(X,Y)$ satisfies\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{X}{2}-3&=12\\\\\\frac{X}{2}&=15\\\\X&=30\\\\Y&=\\frac12(6)-3\\\\Y&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe new coordinates are $(30,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q30-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac13 f\\left(\\frac{x-3}{2}\\right)+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(27,3)$",
          "worked": "Using $f(12)=6$, the new point $(X,Y)$ satisfies\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{X-3}{2}&=12\\\\X-3&=24\\\\X&=27\\\\Y&=\\frac13(6)+1\\\\Y&=3\\end{align*}$$\nThe new coordinates are $(27,3)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
